{"id": "p1_00019", "question": "Bella bought stamps at the post office. Some of the stamps had a snowflake design, some had a truck design, and some had a rose design. Bella bought 11 snowflake stamps. She bought 9 more truck stamps than snowflake stamps, and 13 fewer rose stamps than truck stamps. How many stamps did Bella buy in all?", "trace": "Let's break down the information given in the problem:\n\n* Bella bought 1 eleven stamps with a snowflake designs. So, she bought 11 snowflame stamps.\n* She bought 9 more stamps with a truck design than snowflake design. So, she bought (11 + 9) = 20 truck stamps.\n* she bought 13 fewer stamps with a rose design than truck design. So, she buying 20 - 13 = 7 rose stamps.\n\nIn conclusion, Bella bought a total of 11 + 20 + 7 = 38 stamps. #\n#### 38", "gold_solution": "The number of truck stamps is 11 + 9 = <<11+9=20>>20.\nThe number of rose stamps is 20 - 13 = <<20-13=7>>7.\nBella bought 11 + 20 + 7 = <<11+20+7=38>>38 stamps in all.\n#### 38", "gold_answer": 38.0, "label": "GOOD", "diagnosis": null, "diagnosis_reason": null, "diagnosis_confidence": null, "signals": {"E": 1.0, "V": 1.0, "R": 1.0, "A": 1.0, "G": 1.0, "coherent": true, "correct": true, "final_answer": 38.0, "misses": 0, "bad_eqs": 0, "n_steps": 5, "n_checkpoints": 3, "n_equations": 3, "r_variant": "dup_fraction", "E_struct": 0.6666666666666666, "A_struct": 0.6666666666666666}, "complexity": 3, "stored_at": 1786055744.3258169, "retried": false, "embedding": [-0.010191773064434528, 0.03735741972923279, 0.03578601032495499, 0.023304317146539688, -0.09694626927375793, 0.0604817233979702, -0.014910830184817314, 0.04707272723317146, -0.03397592157125473, -0.07402956485748291, -0.02674301341176033, 0.028860492631793022, 0.003689577803015709, -0.04491947591304779, 0.013016518205404282, 0.011026887223124504, -0.066637322306633, -0.01148225087672472, -0.0876835361123085, 0.004133744165301323, -0.0072685969062149525, -0.09066850692033768, 0.03972695395350456, 0.0662351176